  Anyone use Javacc?  I was wondering if it could parse Lojban.  It's a
  Java-based language parser that also features a tree builder (jjtree).
  I used it to write a complete interpreter for a c-like language.

We've used Javacc.  We did not find it particularly great, and abandoned it=
 for ANTLR.  With great sighs of relief, I might add.

Is there some reason you don't want to use the YACC grammar?  Are you writi=
ng in Java?  You can certainly call C from Java.  Frankly, I prefer functio=
nal languages anyway, and would suggest moving to Haskell and parser contru=
ctors.

Dave Barton


